, brought great glory to this city. On an auspicious day, the lifespan of a fortunate divine soul in the Nalinigulma Vimana (a celestial abode) came to an end, and that soul descended into the womb of Sethani Bhadra. At that very time Mother Bhadra had an auspicious dream. As time passed, on an auspicious day, Sethani Bhadra gave birth to an exceptionally radiant son. The child was named Avantisukumal. Gradually, Avantisukumal grew up. Upon entering youth, he attained mastery in all 72 arts befitting a man; more than that, he also became accomplished in the art of dharma. He was married to 32 maidens as lovely as celestial nymphs.. Once, Acharya Aryasuhastisuri, while sanctifying the earth with his presence, came to Ujjain along with his disciples and stayed in the mansion school of Sethani Bhadra. During the night, the venerable acharya began reciting his study of the Nalinigulma Vimana chapter. At that time, Avantisukumal was seated in a nearby chamber, conversing playfully with his wives. The sound of the acharya's recitation reached Avantisukumal's ears, and he began to think, \\\"Ah! The venerable acharya is describing a scene... I have seen that scene somewhere before\\\" - and as he pondered this, he was instantly overcome with jatismaran gyan (the knowledge of recalling past lives). His previous birth appeared before him as though before his very eyes.. He realized, \\\"Ah! In my past life, I was a god in this very Nalinigulma Vimana. What a vast difference there is between the pleasures there and the pleasures here. The pleasures there are as vast as Mount Meru, while the pleasures here are as small as a mustard seed...\\\" (The page ends here, unfinished, and the story continues on the next page.)\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"1b:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mb-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"a\\\",null,{\\\"href\\\":\\\"https://goo.gl/maps/knDFVAkMNMUMEDkG7\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\